blem "![](images/8e/8eb53506d9e01d09fe3e072a2c6ed1ade05e1cc185693bdd66b34bdf75797ad9.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement “${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x)$ is finite” is false. We get ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x)=-\\infty .$\n\n- Statement “${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}f(x)$ is finite” is true. We get ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}f(x)=3.$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$  has a discontinuity at $x=2$” is true. The function contains a break exactly at $x=2$ and it's impossible to draw its graph without taking our pencil off of the paper."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069367 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1338885-9fa5-56a6-bbde-464a7beff78d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439807} {:answer/id #uuid "c73173bd-c83c-504e-9f9a-d56025e0fdde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c73173bd-c83c-504e-9f9a-d56025e0fdde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439808} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb748d5b-bb9b-5e8c-884e-a291b4ee024f" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is defined at $x = 2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440261} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9689ec4f-c734-5a92-8f3f-3bc8bc7f5697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text}