id #edb/ref 17592186440279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e84c429-d4d2-564d-bd69-f2aa4a25130e" :question/math-academy-id "q-48090" :question/problem "![](images/eb/eb8803dfe4b1af56da4d4942e95d9f34be9afb9130d33c200f8226db3d7277be.png)\n\nWhat are the points of discontinuity of the function plotted above?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The graph breaks at $x=1,2$ and $4$, meaning that we can't draw the plot without taking our pencil off of the paper when passing through these points.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=1,2,4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078487 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f00fd821-a5d4-5844-9db5-795b9e321b94" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Largest Intervals of Continuity of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7332aef-d1ab-59ae-b512-ef545f7ae744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460053} {:answer/id #uuid "a7b71dc6-74e7-5711-981c-28e960d8262e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7332aef-d1ab-59ae-b512-ef545f7ae744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460053} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7e35449-b18a-5d0d-86fa-ec4cdb318007" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-\\infty ,0]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460893} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f03cdec-2456-5c07-b8c8-14bc004724e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460055} {:answer/id #uuid "88b46501-e9aa-54d5-93ba-48e2c0121e50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88b46501-e9aa-54d5-93ba-48e2c0121e50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460056} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea9228a9-88cb-5187-97b8-045712012a79" :answer-field/key "$x\\in [-3,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460894} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c83dd0f1-8727-5449-875d-e38cccc8260e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460057} {:answer/id #uuid "c43d342a-d212-5d50-8724-f2ad92cd2387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c83dd0f1-8727-5449-875d-e38cccc8260e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460057} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3bda150-9207-5a54-ae72-a77156a194f2" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (0,\\infty )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "183472b0-16c2-5809-99fd-33beade724a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-48344" :question/problem "![](images/09/09d006953b4fc1d111a84e78fcc6b2038d53768fb82d6f61a0b2a1d0126bbb40.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ above. On which of the following intervals is the function continuous? \n\nYou may assume that all points of discontinuity of $f(x)$ are shown in the diagram.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement.\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $(-\\infty ,0]$ because it contains a discontinuity at $x=-3.$\n\n- The function is continuous on $[-3,2].$ It is continuous on $(-3,2),$ and also right continuous at $x=-3$ and left continuous at $x=2.$\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $(0,\\infty )$ because it contains a discontinuity at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in [-3,2]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078487 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f00fd821-a5d4-5844-9db5-795b9e321b94" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Largest Intervals of Continuity of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1abb4819-32aa-5825-8aba-4fd7804637a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460059} {:answer/id #uuid "f35e1f11-2422-51e5-af6e-1235b12fd7b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1abb4819-32aa-5825-8aba-4fd7804637a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460059} :answer-field/id #uuid "43e016e3-9a6a-572e-859b-c5130dd62a24" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460896} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1283eade-08fd-5f30-9ef4-1519d117e848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460061} {:answer/id #uuid "c48d2474-80c0-579a-8b13-6c238bde32de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c48d2474-80c0-579a-8b13-6c238bde32de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460062} :answer-field/id #uuid "10869229-edc0-5347-81f2-236b0b2ae409" :answer-field/key "$x\\in [1,\\infty )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460897} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44d75c89-61f0-52fb-8cb7-770f1e35dd76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460063} {:answer/id #uuid "47fa91ad-b6ac-59f1-821a-07abc46f5379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47fa91ad-b6ac-59f1-821a-07abc46f5379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460064} :answer-field/id #uuid "14b6deca-6eac-566a-af42-c9c053359ec1" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-1,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5bbc454b-136b-559e-ae09-8d1685b0819e" :question/math-academy-id "q-48346" :question/problem "![](images/ff/ff6f5e2fbd530ee9d90c2adf02bb212886fb137c1d55c9e9d78958902ccc9f13.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ above. On which of the following intervals is the function continuous? \n\nYou may assume that all points of discontinuity of $f(x)$ are shown in the diagram.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement.\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $(-\\infty ,1].$ Although the function is continuous on $(-\\infty ,1),$ it is not left-continuous at $x=1.$\n\n- The function is continuous on $[1,\\infty ).$ It is continuous on $(1,\\infty )$ and also right continuous at $x=1.$\n\n- The function is continuous on $(-1,1).$ It is continuous on $(-\\infty ,1)$ and this contains the interval $(-1,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in [1,\\infty )$; $x\\in (-1,1)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083612 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12a5ad95-0cc9-53c5-8e1c-dae35d1c4447" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Points Where the Normal is Horizontal or Vertical"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0735403-c4cc-5f1c-b3f3-f20e814b4e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439583} {:answer/id #uuid "18c5b8fc-dc2a-5f66-aba9-2fb2139b0e8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18c5b8fc-dc2a-5f66-aba9-2fb2139b0e8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439584} :answer-field/id #uuid "45f84d85-7a93-543f-94bb-a475c80511cd" :answer-field/key "$t=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440149} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7325a515-140f-5d60-bed7-46dc88237008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439585} {:answer/id #uuid "76c0b0ff-3576-50aa-ae9a-450fb61d13ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76c0b0ff-3576-50aa-ae9a-450fb61d13ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439586} :answer-field/id #uuid "23d3ed3a-04d8-5745-91e6-80f3e4c230a7" :answer-field/key "$t=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a631b20-d142-5c85-8a98-edc055f0d25f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439587} {:answer/id #uuid "2b5cc863-692b-5dad-a794-3874acf00aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a631b20-d142-5c85-8a98-edc055f0d25f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439587} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc1b0da1-c6f8-5d48-bed9-a7f7760363df" :answer-field/key "$t=\\pi$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440151}] :question/id #uuid "57cb918d-01c6-5793-92dd-c253fd54156c" :question/math-academy-id "q-21080" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n$x = 4\\cos 2t + 5, y = 5\\sin 2t + 4, 0 \\le t < π$.\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the normal to the curve is horizontal.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A vertical tangent (and horizontal normal) requires x′(t)=0 and y′(t)≠0. Here $x′(t)=- 8 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}$ and $y′(t)=10 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}$. Within the given half-open interval the solutions are $\\left\\{0, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right\\}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083613 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083278 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fc81cba-b997-54bc-9e11-0a4ff130833e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Points Where the Tangent is Horizontal or Vertical"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "511bd910-5bb8-5b0b-90bc-975fb41660b0"